I just filled my A2000 up with memory (9.5 megs), created a HUGE Rad: (*)
(6.5 megs), installed Nethack there and play from the icon for weeks
at a time with no problems and no loading delays.  Of course, I back
up "record" (the score file) and the files in the "bones" directory
and any save file onto a floppy once in a while in case of a power
outage, but that's the only overhead.

I keep the whole nethack directory plus a nethack.info drawer file in
a nh309.zoo file that fits very comfortably (612Kbytes) on a single
floppy and loads back into Rad:, when I have to rebuild after a cold
reboot, in about three minutes.

A really pleasent way to get offed by monsters an average of once every
five minutes (used to be once a minute, I'm improving!), and the extra
memory has lots of other uses when I can tear myself away from Nethack.

Just a suggestion for the permanently Amiga Nethack addicted.

